    "interpretation": "Observed corr(log area, log unit price) = -0.547. Under the shuffled-price placebo the same statistic is -0.466 (95% band -0.468..-0.464), so about 85% of the observed association is the mechanical ratio effect. The elasticity estimate (log price on log area, within postcode and year) is 0.244 with a test of beta=1 giving p=0; a slope below 1 means unit price genuinely falls with size once location and time are held fixed."
